## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over multiple segments with a budget and in/out state tracking to allow adjacency.

## Key Concepts
- DP with segment count and in/out state
- Transitions for starting, extending, and ending a segment
- Handling adjacency and at-most-k constraint

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(a, k){
  const n = a.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  // dp[i][t][s] -> max sum using first i elements
  let dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array.from({length: k+1}, ()=> [NEG, NEG]));
  dp[0][0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      for(let s=0;s<2;s++){
        const cur = dp[i][t][s];
        if(cur===NEG) continue;
        if(s===0){
          // skip a[i]
          dp[i+1][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t][0], cur);
          // start new
          if(t<k) dp[i+1][t+1][1] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t+1][1], cur + a[i]);
        } else {
          // extend
          dp[i+1][t][1] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t][1], cur + a[i]);
          // end
          dp[i+1][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i+1][t][0], cur);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let ans = 0;
  for(let t=0;t<=k;t++) ans = Math.max(ans, dp[n][t][0], dp[n][t][1]);
  return ans;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP with non-uniform skip constraints and reconstruction, common in scheduling and resource-constrained selection. It ensures you can encode constraints as a forward DP and extract the chosen indices.

## Key Concepts

- DP with forward state (i, r)
- Transition skipping vs taking with jump i+gap[i]
- Path reconstruction and complexity

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxSumWithGaps(A, gap, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const memo = Array.from({ length: n + 2 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(null));

  const go = (i, r) => {
    if (r === 0) return 0;
    if (i > n) return NEG;
    if (memo[i][r] != null) return memo[i][r];
    const skip = go(i + 1, r);
    const take = A[i - 1] + go(Math.min(n + 1, i + gap[i - 1]), r - 1);
    const best = Math.max(skip, take);
    memo[i][r] = best;
    return best;
  };

  const best = go(1, k);
  return { best, memo };
}
```

